# Database Schema Rules

## Change Protocol (All 3 Steps Required)

1. `supabase/core.sql` ← source of truth, bump version
2. `src/lib/schemaVersion.ts` ← sync EXPECTED_SCHEMA_VERSION
3. `src/types/supabase.ts` ← regenerate with `npm run gen:types`

## Supabase Query Patterns

```typescript
// GOOD: explicit columns, error handling
const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from('files')
  .select('id, name, status')
  .range(0, 49);
if (error) throw error;

// BAD: select(*), no error check
const { data } = await supabase.from('files').select('*');
```

## Storage

- Private files: signed URLs only
- Public assets: direct URLs OK

## No Migration Files

This project has no `migrations/` directory and no dated migration files. Do not create
either, and do not follow a `YYYYMMDD-description.sql` convention — nothing in this repo
reads one.

`supabase/core.sql` and `supabase/modules/*.sql` are the source of truth and are edited in
place. Every file is idempotent (`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, `DROP POLICY IF EXISTS`
before `CREATE POLICY`, enum creation and FK additions wrapped in exception-handling `DO`
blocks), so a fresh install and an upgrade are the same operation: run the whole edited
file in the Supabase SQL editor. There is no delta to write, which is why the workflow
below says to run the full schema file.

`schema_version` and `EXPECTED_SCHEMA_VERSION` do the job a migration ledger would
otherwise do — they are how the app decides whether a database is current, so bumping both
is not optional (see Change Protocol above).

Building a database from nothing means running `core.sql`, then `10-source-files.sql`,
`15-inspection.sql`, `20-change-control.sql`, `30-supply-chain.sql`,
`40-integrations.sql`, `50-extensions.sql`, `60-customers.sql`. Modules `10` and `15` are
both required despite `15` being numbered like an optional one — `checkin_file()` in
module 10 queries tables that module 15 creates. See `supabase/README.md`.

## Schema Change Workflow

When making schema changes:
- **Only** update the schema files (`supabase/core.sql`, `supabase/modules/*.sql`)
- **Never** provide migration SQL in code blocks — user runs the full schema file
- **Never** run terminal commands to push SQL to Supabase
- Just update the files and confirm it's done